# Market data vendor (prices, fundamentals, statements) — https://twelvedata.com
# ADX and DFM publish no public data feed, so quotes come from this licensed vendor. Without a key the
# markets pages still list every ADX/DFM stock and show DFM filings, but prices/indicators show "not connected".
TWELVEDATA_API_KEY=
# Requests per minute allowed by your plan (free = 8). Raise it on paid plans so the board loads faster.
TWELVEDATA_RPM=8
# Dev only: synthetic, clearly-labelled test data so the UI can be developed without a key. Ignored in production.
# GD_FIXTURES=1

# Model provider for the simple AI routes (briefs, prep packs, stance reads, Ask, world brief, agent plan/compose).
# Unset or "anthropic": Claude, as before. "hf": Hugging Face Inference Providers (DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, roughly 8-10x cheaper than Sonnet).
# The councils, dossier, desk, bird audit and research note also move to HF, but they need web search, and Anthropic's built-in search does not exist there:
# set TAVILY_API_KEY (https://tavily.com) or those runs work from the collected facts only and say so. No batch transport and no prompt-cache sharing on HF.
# LLM_PROVIDER=hf
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...          # a fine-grained token with only the "Make calls to Inference Providers" permission
# TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...
# HF_MODEL=deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash:cheapest   # any HF model id; ":cheapest" / ":fastest" / ":<provider>" pick the provider

# AI research tab. Credentials resolve in this order: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, or your `ant auth login` profile
# (a profile is already active on this machine, so nothing is needed in dev). Each note bills your Anthropic account.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# RESEARCH_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5   # default; Opus costs about twice as much per token
# RESEARCH_EFFORT=medium             # low | medium | high | xhigh | max
# RESEARCH_MAX_RUN_USD=1             # hard ceiling per note in US dollars (default 1, never above 5)
# RESEARCH_MAX_PER_HOUR=6            # server-wide cap on new notes
# RESEARCH_ENABLED=0                 # set to 0 to switch the feature off
# AI country briefs (no web tools; about $0.015 each on the default model; cached 3 h; start only on click)
# BRIEF_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# The country brief and the prep pack cost about 4 and 6 cents on Sonnet. claude-haiku-5-5 cuts that by about 70 percent (1.2 and 1.6 cents) and writes a close second-best, but in testing it once named the wrong weakest aspect of the scorecard, so Sonnet is the default. Set BRIEF_MODEL / PREP_MODEL to try it.
# BRIEF_MAX_PER_HOUR=20              # server-wide cap on new (uncached) briefs
# BRIEF_ENABLED=0                    # set to 0 to switch briefs off
# DOSSIER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5    # detailed ministerial and desk briefings (read the web); Opus costs about twice as much
# DOSSIER_EFFORT=                    # leave empty for low (short runs) or medium (long runs); low | medium | high | xhigh | max
# DOSSIER_MAX_RUN_USD=1              # hard ceiling per briefing run in US dollars (default 1, never above 5)
# DOSSIER_MAX_PER_HOUR=4             # server-wide cap on new detailed briefings
# DOSSIER_ENABLED=0                  # set to 0 to switch them off

# Optional free keys that switch on key-gated layers (each shows a clear message until set)
# AISSTREAM_API_KEY=           # live vessels (AIS): https://aisstream.io
# WINDY_WEBCAMS_API_KEY=       # public webcams: https://api.windy.com/webcams
